 # Prefer Type Over Interface Rule

Consider using `type` instead of `interface` for this type definition. When you need to merging or inherit use intersections.

## Examples

### ❌ Bad
```typescript
interface UserData {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    age: number;
}
```

### ✅ Good
```typescript
type UserData = {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    age: number;
};
```